pgRouting 3.4.1: where its source is, and a written offer of it
================================================================

This image carries the binaries of pgRouting 3.4.1: the extension pgrouting. pgRouting is
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later, with some parts under the
Boost Software License or the MIT licence. Its licence is in this folder (LICENSE).

The binaries come unmodified from the base image supabase/postgres:17.6.1.175. Aber does not
modify or rebuild them, and Aber's migrations do not create this extension. This applies to the
three images built on that base: ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/supabase-db,
ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/db-init and ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/backup-service.


Download the source
-------------------

Aber mirrors the complete corresponding source of pgRouting 3.4.1, its patch and the scripts
that built it, one archive each, with a SHA256SUMS file, in a GitHub release of its own:
https://github.com/Harri-Llewelyn/Aber/releases/tag/gpl-sources-supabase-postgres-17.6.1.175-postgis
It covers every Aber image built on supabase/postgres:17.6.1.175.


Where the source is upstream
----------------------------

- pgRouting v3.4.1:
  https://github.com/pgRouting/pgrouting/tree/v3.4.1
- The one patch the base image's build applies to it, for PostgreSQL 17:
  https://github.com/supabase/postgres/blob/17.6.1.175/nix/ext/pgrouting/pgrouting-3.4.1-pg17.patch
- The scripts that built it, in supabase/postgres at 17.6.1.175 (nix/ext/pgrouting/):
  https://github.com/supabase/postgres/tree/17.6.1.175
  and the nixpkgs its flake.lock pins, which supplies Boost 1.87.0, whose graph headers are
  compiled in (Boost Software License 1.0):
  https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/tree/fb7944c166a3b630f177938e478f0378e64ce108

pgRouting's library loads nothing the PostgreSQL server does not load already.


The written offer
-----------------

For three years from the date of each Aber release that ships this image, Aber's maintainer will
give anyone who asks a complete machine-readable copy of the corresponding source code of
pgRouting 3.4.1 as built in this image, with the patch and the scripts that built it. The charge
is no more than the cost of making the copy.

To ask, use GitHub's private vulnerability reporting for Aber:
https://github.com/Harri-Llewelyn/Aber/security/advisories/new
(the Security tab, then Report a vulnerability). The form is built for vulnerability reports.
Use it for a source request too. Say in it:

- which image you have and its tag, the Aber release (for example
  ghcr.io/harri-llewelyn/aber/supabase-db);
- that this is a request for the GPL source of pgRouting.

The request opens a draft advisory that only Aber's maintainers can see.
